   NAME
	Python - Python 2.7.18 interpreter for classic AmigaOS.

   FORMAT
	Python [options] [-c cmd | -m mod | file | -] [arg ...]

   TEMPLATE
	-c/K,-m/K,FILE,ARGS/M,-i/S,-S/S,-E/S,-O/S,-OO/S,-B/S,-s/S,-u/S,
	-v/S,-V/S,-W/K,-x/S,-3/S,-Q/K,-?/S

   PATH
	(this drawer)/Python
	Optional: ASSIGN Python: (this drawer) ; PATH Python: ADD

   FUNCTION
	Python is an interpreted, interactive, object-oriented language.
	This Amiga port is based on Python 2.7.18 (amigazen project),
	continuing Irmen de Jong's classic AmigaPython line.

	Copy this entire drawer anywhere and run Python from Shell or
	Workbench.  No installer is required.  The standard library is
	loaded from lib/ next to the binary:

		lib/python27.zip
		lib/lib-dynload/
		lib/site-python/

	Optional ASSIGN Python: to this drawer is only a convenience so
	you can type "Python" from any directory and set Default Tool
	to Python:Python on project icons.

	Shell:

		Python                 interactive console
		Python script.py       run a script
		Python -c "print 1"    run a command string
		Python -?              short help / usage

	Workbench:

		Double-click Python for a CON: console.
		Project icons: set Default Tool to this Python (or
		Python:Python).  The project file is the script.
		Close the console with the close gadget or Ctrl+C.

	Environment (optional):

		PYTHONHOME   override prefix
		PYTHONPATH   semicolon-separated module search dirs
		PYTHONCASEOK relax import filename case matching
		TZ / locale  timezone (see Help/Amiga)

	Documentation in this drawer:

		Python.help                 this file
		Help/AmigaPython.guide      Amiga port guide
		Help/DiveIntoPython/        Dive Into Python tutorial
		Help/Amiga/                 Amiga module notes (reST)
		README                      quick start
		Help/DISCL_and_COPYRIGHT    licenses / disclaimer

	Upstream language and library reference:
		https://docs.python.org/2.7/

	amigazen project:
		https://github.com/amigazen/amigapython/
		http://www.amigazen.com/amigapython/

	Networking needs bsdsocket.library (e.g. Roadshow).  I-Net225
	is not supported.  pwd/grp/crypt may need usergroup.library.

	See also: Help/AmigaPython.guide
